      "*Suo* means both *his* and *her*: *Marco {ip:ama} la sua casa. Anna {ip:ama} la sua casa.*",
      "With a single family member, leave out the article: *mia madre, tuo fratello*. Keep it in the plural (*i miei fratelli*) and with *loro* (*la loro madre*).",
      "To compare two things, use *più… di* (more… than), *meno… di* (less… than) and *come* (as).",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Form",
            "Example",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "più + adjective + di",
              "Roma {ip:è} più grande di Pisa.",
              "Rome is bigger than Pisa."
            ],
            [
              "meno + adjective + di",
              "Pisa {ip:è} meno grande di Roma.",
              "Pisa is less big than Rome."
            ],
            [
              "adjective + come",
              "Anna {ip:è} alta come Sara.",
              "Anna is as tall as Sara."
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "*Di* joins with the article: *più grande **della** tua casa, più caro **del** pane*."
    ]
